    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d736">

                <pb facs="0777" n="769" xml:id="pg769"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.00/9076</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Vice Consul at Valencia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wallner</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Valencia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-03-28T13:00:00-04:30">March 28, 1939—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 2:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>35. Ugarte<anchor n="48" xml:id="d736-f1"/> has just telephoned to report that
                    Madrid was surrendered this morning by the National Defense Council whose
                    members have all departed except Besteiro. The entry of the Nationalist troops
                    is expected this afternoon but the city is already bedecked with Nationalist
                    flags. There are no disorders and all Americans are believed safe.</p>
                <p>Valencia quiet.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wallner</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d736-f1" n="48" xml:id="d736-f1-content">
                <p>Custodian of American Embassy premises at Madrid.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
